### CSRF Protection Tests for FORUM.KG
### Tests cookie-based CSRF protection

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3002
@phone = +996555200300

### Test 1: Get CSRF token (should succeed)
# @name getCsrfToken
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/csrf-token

### Extract CSRF token from response
@csrfToken = {{getCsrfToken.response.body.csrfToken}}

### Test 2: POST without CSRF token (should fail with 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/request-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "purpose": "LOGIN"
}

### Expected: 403 CSRF_TOKEN_INVALID

### Test 3: POST with CSRF token in header (should succeed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/request-otp
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "purpose": "LOGIN"
}

### Expected: 200 OK with challengeId

### Test 4: POST with wrong CSRF token (should fail with 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/request-otp
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: wrong-token-12345678901234567890123456789012

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "purpose": "LOGIN"
}

### Expected: 403 CSRF_TOKEN_INVALID

### Test 5: GET request without CSRF token (should succeed - safe method)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session

### Expected: 401 UNAUTHORIZED (no CSRF error, just not authenticated)

### Test 6: POST with cross-origin (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/request-otp
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: https://evil-site.com
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "purpose": "LOGIN"
}

### Expected: 403 CSRF_TOKEN_INVALID (Origin validation fails)

### Test 7: Complete OTP flow with CSRF
# 7.1 Get CSRF token
# @name getToken
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/csrf-token

@token = {{getToken.response.body.csrfToken}}

# 7.2 Request OTP with CSRF token
# @name requestOTP
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/request-otp
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{token}}

{
  "phone": "+996555200301",
  "purpose": "LOGIN"
}

@challengeId = {{requestOTP.response.body.challengeId}}

# 7.3 Verify OTP (need to get actual code from DB)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/verify-otp
# Content-Type: application/json
# X-CSRF-Token: {{token}}
#
# {
#   "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}",
#   "code": "123456"
# }

### Test 8: Logout with CSRF token
# First need to be authenticated, then:
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
# X-CSRF-Token: {{token}}

### Expected: 200 OK, CSRF token cleared

### Test 9: Test CSRF token after logout (should get new token)
# GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/csrf-token
### Expected: 200 OK with new token (different from previous)

### Test 10: Multiple concurrent requests with same token
# All should succeed if token is valid
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/request-otp
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "phone": "+996555200302",
  "purpose": "LOGIN"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/request-otp
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "phone": "+996555200303",
  "purpose": "LOGIN"
}

### Both should succeed - CSRF token is reusable within session
